  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3_solu_chem_pa1_3.jpg\"/></p><p>(M) and (N) are identical meso compounds</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3_solu_chem_pa1_2.jpg\"/></p><p>(O) and (P) are enantiomers</p><p><strong>Explanation of 4 options :</strong></p><p>(i) (M) and (O) are distereomers of each other.</p><p>(N) and (P) are distereomers of each other.</p><p>(ii) Addition of <math><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> on alkene follows non-classical carbocation mechanism. It is anti or trans addition.</p><p>(iii) (O) and (P) are enantiomers</p><p>(iv) (M) and (N) are identical and (O) and (P) are enantiomers.</p><p>(M and O) are distereomers and (N and P) are distereomers.</p>",
    "image": null
